        "prompt": "List the elements of set $P$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P=\\{11,15\\}$",
          "worked": "The elements inside the circle $P$ are 11 and 15, so $P=\\{11,15\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Sven says that 11 is not an element of set $Q$. Is Sven correct?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No. $11\\in Q$.",
          "worked": "Sven is incorrect. The circle $P$ is inside $Q$, so 11 is also an element of $Q$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Write down the elements of set $Q$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$Q=\\{11,12,13,14,15,16,17,18\\}$",
          "worked": "Include every element inside the oval $Q$, including those in $P$: $Q=\\{11,12,13,14,15,16,17,18\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "How many elements are not in set $Q$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "1",
          "worked": "Only 19 lies outside $Q$, so there is 1 element not in $Q$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "How many elements are not in set $P$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "7",
          "worked": "The elements outside $P$ are $\\{12,13,14,16,17,18,19\\}$, so there are 7.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q2-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "Explain why the elements in “both $P$ and $Q$” are the same as those of set $P$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P\\subseteq Q$, so $P\\cap Q=P$.",
          "worked": "Every element of $P$ is also in $Q$ because $P$ lies entirely inside $Q$. Therefore $P\\subseteq Q$ and $P\\cap Q=P$.",
